 "statement": {
  "status": "present",
  "value": "Codec() has encode(nums) and decode(runs). encode scans nums left to right: every maximal run of at least 3 equal values becomes \"RLE[value, count]\"; the remaining values between such runs are grouped, in order, into chunks of at most 8 values, each written \"BP[width, v1, ..., vk]\" where width is the largest bit length among the chunk's values (at least 1). decode(runs) expands each \"RLE[value, count]\" into count copies of value and each \"BP[width, v1, ..., vk]\" into v1..vk, concatenated in order. Items are separated by \", \".",
  "provenance": [
   {
    "repository": "gamma",
    "revision": null,
    "path": "projects/algorithm_solver/catalogue/authored/hack2hire-chunk10-b-20261028-v1/contracts.json",
